      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled outpatient dose is 3,200 mg/day, and inpatient use is generally the same.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400-600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (typical for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you want the dose exactly as written, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical reason. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to review it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
